WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.880
Koizumi-san!

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.120
Want to go to karaoke with us? Our treat.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:10.860
I've got these movie tickets. Want to come?

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.170
There's this café with great desserts.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.080
I got free tickets to an amusement park.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.320
The guys are really going 
after Koizumi lately.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.750
It pisses me off.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.300
Sure. She's been here for a while now,
but she's still single.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.560
Those poor boys.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.950
They can ask her out all 
they want, but it's no use.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.840
<b>Ahh</b>

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.920
Koizumi-san's only lover is ramen!

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.980
I know this all too well.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.270
Why do you sound so condescending?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.630
I guess you'll have to do. 
Misa-chan, want to come?

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:45.640
How dare you?!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.850
Invite <i>me</i> first, or forget it!

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:51.240
Koizumi-san, let's walk home.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.150
Together!

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.670
No, thank you.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.180
I have plans.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.420
See? She's a very shy person.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.330
"See" what, exactly?

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.260
You think Koizumi-san has a boyfriend?

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.570
She has to. There's no way 
a girl that cute is single.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.340
<i>They really don't get it.</i>

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>The only company she seeks out is ramen.</i>

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.060
<i>Ramen and nothing else!</i>

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.250
I have plans.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:23.950
I have plans.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.830
I have plans.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:25.940
I have plans.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:33.480
<i>It must be... ramen, and nothing... else.</i>

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.740
Sorry! I'm going home!

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:37.600
That was fast.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.470
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:57.010
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:57.930
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.960
<b>Western Restaurant</b>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.210
<b>Nihonbashi</b>

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.170
<i>It must be ramen, and nothing else.</i>

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:22.470
<i>Ramen...</i>

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.510
You think Koizumi-san has a boyfriend?

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.520
She has to. There's no way 
a girl that cute is single.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.940
<i>Koizumi could never go out with some guy.</i>

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.440
<i>The only love for her is ramen.</i>

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.190
<i>She must have come to this 
business district for...</i>

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.450
<i>a ramen shop!</i>

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.830
<i>I-It's not a ramen shop?!</i>

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.010
<i>Koizumi-san going to a fancy, 
retro Western restaurant?</i>

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:54.720
You're late!

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.000
<i>This feels so wrong!</i>

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.580
Sorry. Were you waiting long?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.590
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.330
<i>Could she really be meeting some guy?</i>

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.730
<i>She keeps checking the time and looking around.</i>

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:10.230
<i>And what's with that "lovestruck maiden" look?</i>

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.700
<i>Adorable!</i>

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.400
<i>Wait, no!</i>

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.360
<i>Her in a high-profile celebrity 
area like this can only mean...</i>

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.510
<i>She's seeing an older man!</i>

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.000
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.480
Let me introduce you to something 
lovelier than ramen.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.040
<i>I won't allow it.</i>

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.120
<i>I won't allow it!</i>

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.680
I will never, ever, ever,
ever, ever, ever, ever...

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.130
Thanks for waiting.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.160
Sorry for being late.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.220
It's fine.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.850
<i>It really is some guy!</i>

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.360
<i>No, no, no, no, no, no, no!</i>

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.340
Hey there!

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.300
Sorry about the wait.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.280
We're really sorry.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.730
<i>Not just one, but a whole bunch of guys!</i>

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.740
<i>Could she actually be seeing multiple guys?</i>

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.210
<i>No!</i>

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:05.940
<i>You can't do that, Koizumi-san!</i>

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.890
<i>Koizumi-san! Koizumi-san!</i>

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.550
Koizumi-san!

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.450
You have to stop!

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:19.210
Koizumi-san, that's really wrong!

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.620
Uh, well, we should be going.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:27.590
Yeah.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.600
Sorry we made you wait.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.600
Man, I'm full.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.330
No problem.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.860
Well, back to work.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.660
Huh? What?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.380
You weren't here to meet with those people?

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.100
What are you talking about?

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:44.030
I was just waiting for them 
to leave their space.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.530
<i>Their space?</i>

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.660
<b>-men</b>

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:51.240
Taimeiken

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:51.740
Taimeiken

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:57.960
Y-You're saying that behind this Western
restaurant, there's a stand-up ramen shop?!

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.250
What is this?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:03.250
<b>Ramen 
Corner</b>

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.250
As the name suggests, this is a ramen corner.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:06.750
I arrived at the same time 
as that group of four,

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.160
and since there are only four 
spots inside, I let them go first.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:12.510
Oh...

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.220
So that's what it was.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:16.640
Anyway...

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.090
Why are you here, anyway?

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:25.870
Well, uh...

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:33.250
I'm going to have ramen, as I had planned.

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:34.240
What about you?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.370
Me, too!

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:46.880
You can see the entire 
kitchen from the counter!

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.010
A chashu ramen with borscht 
and coleslaw, right?

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.240
With borscht and coleslaw?

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.220
I'm going to get that, too.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.480
<b>Coleslaw</b>

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.560
<b>Borscht</b>

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.620
Here's mine.

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.870
Here you go. Borscht with coleslaw.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.530
The food looks so Western!

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.310
This is so good!

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.480
It's so good, I wouldn't be surprised 
if they charged way more!

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.810
I always order this when I come here.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.040
Oh, you can see into the 
restaurant from here.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.240
By the way, you can order ramen in there, too.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.360
Then why'd you stand outside 
waiting to get in here?

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.520
Because...

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:35.120
I prefer the atmosphere in here.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.130
One butter ramen and one chashu ramen.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:43.400
Wow, this looks great!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.770
Let's eat.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:10.170
So good!

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.660
The butter melts into the soup.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.790
This is the first time I've eaten 
standing up, and it's not bad at all.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:26.020
I finally got to eat this.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.180
I guess ramen really is your lover, huh?

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:35.990
What are you talking about?

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:37.860
Nothing!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.700
Hey, why are you so far away, anyway?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.900
It's not necessary to stand side-by-side.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.420
What?!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.210
<b>Kyoto Ramen</b>

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.290
<b>Hakata Ramen</b>

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:51.800
Fatback...

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:56.800
<b>This area is
Koizumi-san's
"Temptation Alley"</b>

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.160
Green onion...

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.360
Tonkotsu...

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:56.800
I'll go with you, Koizumi-san!

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.810
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:06.810
<b>Red or White</b>

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:13.840
How does this look?

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.520
Oh, looks great.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.360
White looks a little too good on me.
You don't think it looks too plain?

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.080
I don't think so at all. It's perfect.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:25.350
What about this one?

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.620
That looks great, too.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.420
Red looks good on me, too!

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.800
But I feel like it's a little too aggressive.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.140
Yeah, it's really cute.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.980
This red one is cute...

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:40.080
But I do want a white summer outfit, too.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.860
Hey, Yuu, which one do you like better?

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:45.730
I think they're both great.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.890
Hey! Yuu, are you even looking?

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.650
I am looking.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:54.010
This mannequin looks like Koizumi-san.

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.150
Ugh! Yuu!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.160
Jeez...

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.580
I invited you to go shopping because
you said Koizumi-san ran away from you.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.910
That's not true.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.630
We were walking home together, 
and I lost sight of her, that's all.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.620
<b>Bzz Bzz</b>

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:09.960
<b>Where are you?</b>

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:09.960
<b>Misa...</b>

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:11.130
<b>Huh...</b>

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.060
You mean she ran away.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:18.270
Well, we've come all this way, 
so you're coming over, right?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:19.760
If it's not a bother.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.050
My mom's at a class reunion.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.390
It's early, but want to get some dinner first?

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:25.590
Sounds good.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:26.640
Where should we go?

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:30.740
That new place by the shopping district 
has been getting rave reviews.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.380
Their buckwheat flour crêpes 
are supposed to be amazing!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:34.500
Want to check it out?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:37.990
Oh... Well...

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.940
We're having ramen?

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:47.830
Yeah!

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.900
Their sign for tonkotsu ramen
 just looked so good!

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.860
Seriously, Yuu, Koizumi 
has totally poisoned you.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.840
If someone mentions tonkotsu ramen,
I can't hold back.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.450
I'm on a diet right now, you know.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.960
I would've liked something 
lighter and trendier.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.970
But isn't this place pretty trendy, Misa-san?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.350
The music they're playing is hip.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:13.770
And look, they're not serving regular water. 
You get this delicious-smelling tea.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.360
This is so cool!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.420
I guess.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.840
Care for a glass?

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.220
Thanks.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.360
Oh, this is rooibos tea.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.320
So, what are you getting?

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.780
Something spicy. Something really spicy!

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.470
That was fast.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:33.040
<b>Akamaru
Modern</b>

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.930
I guess I'll get...

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:35.040
<b>Shiromaru
Classic</b>

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.540
Red or white, huh?

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:37.420
<b>A Bowl of Origins</b>

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:37.420
"A bowl of origins" or "a bowl of innovation."

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.420
<b>A Bowl of Innovation</b>

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.690
I can never make up my mind 
about stuff like this...

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.110
Hurry up.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:43.220
Wait, what did Koizumi-san 
say that one time?

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:47.170
When I'm in a new restaurant, 
I start with their basic items.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.100
<i>If I follow her advice, I should order 
the "origins" with the white broth.</i>

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.500
<i>But she also said...</i>

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.140
But it's not wrong to aggressively go 
for the item that interests you most.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.860
<i>If I go that route, it's the 
"innovation" with the red broth.</i>

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.490
<b>White</b>

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.490
<b>The 
Original</b>

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:00.490
<i>Origins?</i>

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.110
<b>Red</b>

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.110
<b>The
Innovation</b>

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:02.110
<i>Or innovation?</i>

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:06.210
What would Koizumi-san pick?

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:09.480
I wish you'd put that much 
thought into my outfits.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.040
Red, I think.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.540
I always take an aggressive 
stance, Koizumi-san.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.500
All right, I get it. You want red.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.240
Excuse me! Can we order, please?

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:22.130
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:26.560
Hey, do you think we're allowed 
to eat these bean sprouts?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.930
I don't see why not.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.270
Wait, is this all-you-can-eat bean sprouts?!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.930
They're nice and spicy!

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:36.210
I love this!

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:38.480
This could be a side dish on its own!

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.490
But aren't we supposed 
to put them on our ramen?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.210
I'm sure it's not a problem 
if we snack on them a little.

00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:47.010
Besides, they say that if you 
eat bean sprouts before a meal,

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:49.600
it helps absorb excess fat.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.950
It's kind of like that 
"low insulin diet" thing.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.750
Plus, the capsaicin in red pepper 
helps metabolize the fats faster,

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.230
and the rooibos tea inhibits fat storage.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.000
It's perfect!

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.630
Wow, you're a real expert
when it comes to beauty.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:03.970
Just leave it to me.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.800
Thank you for waiting.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:08.350
Here it is.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.100
One Karaka ramen and one Akamaru ramen.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:22.980
Let's eat!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.680
Extra Noodles  (Thin Hakata noodles)

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.680
<b>Regular</b>

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.680
<b>yen / Small</b>

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.680
<b>yen</b>

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.320
Oh, you can get extra noodles here.

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.680
I think I'll get some.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.450
This is pretty light for tonkotsu. 
I feel like I could eat more.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:58.140
Want to get some extra noodles and split them?

00:13:58.140 --> 00:14:00.400
Aren't you on a diet?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.820
I ate the bean sprouts, so I'm fine!

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.990
Good point.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:09.410
<b>Ippudo</b>

00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.360
I'm stuffed.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.410
That was so good.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.210
It hit the spot.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.510
But eating that spicy food made 
me want something sweet.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.070
What about your diet?

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:18.420
I drank that rooibos tea, so I'm fine.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.250
Wanna buy some cake at the 
station and take it home, then?

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:22.610
Sounds good!

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:37.160
One Shiromaru Classic with 
a side of mentaiko rice.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.280
Time to eat.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:21.850
Excuse me.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.500
I'd like extra noodles and 
an order of one-bite gyoza.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.480
Coming right up!

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.200
<b>That's right,</b>

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.200
<b>ramen truly is</b>

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.830
<i>The</i> source of energy.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:38.950
<b><i>the</i> source of energy</b>

00:15:36.970 --> 00:15:38.950
<b>Don't you think so?</b>

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.960
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.950
<b>Convenience Store</b>

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:57.100
<i>Today's mock exam didn't go that well.</i>

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:02.850
<i>I was so nervous, I didn't eat anything 
all day, but I'm also not hungry at all.</i>

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.110
<i>I'll buy a drink and go home.</i>

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:09.660
<i>It's still far away,</i>

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:14.000
<i>but I already get depressed thinking 
about entrance exams and career planning.</i>

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.990
Welcome!

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.420
<i>Maybe I just worry too much.</i>

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:23.620
Koizumi-san?

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.760
What are you doing here on a Sunday?

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:30.000
I like their eat-in corner.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.350
Uh, that doesn't answer my question.

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:37.230
I changed my regular plan for today and 
came to enjoy convenience store ramen.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:38.150
This is paper trash.

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.310
<i>She wasn't lying.</i>

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.390
<i>She has several empty containers already.</i>

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.740
<i>An unwavering appetite for ramen...</i>

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.430
<i>And she's still eating more?</i>

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:51.040
I'm going now.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:51.820
Sure.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:54.260
<i>As curt as ever.</i>

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:58.860
I never thought of convenience stores as 
having a particularly good ramen selection.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:16:59.950
They do.

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:03.190
You can divide convenience store 
ramen into roughly three types.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:05.200
First, there's the refrigerated kind.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:08.050
Ranging from microwaveable 
ones with lots of toppings,

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:11.100
to uncooked noodles meant 
to be prepared at home.

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:11.890
<i>Uh-oh...</i>

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.840
<i>Looks like I triggered something.</i>

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.160
Next, there's frozen ramen, 
which is quite popular recently.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:21.050
Due to recent advances in technology, 
the freezing and thawing doesn't affect

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:27.440
We recommend microwaving this!
* Please place the product on a microwave-safe dish with <b><u>this side up</u></b>.
* When handling the dish, please be careful not to burn yourself.

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:24.540
the texture or flavor of the noodles,
 so they can be enjoyed to their full potential.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:27.440
What's more, their price-performance
ratio is outstanding.

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:29.840
This is true even though the alkaline water

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.320
in the noodles is sensitive 
to temperature changes.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.710
Extraordinary, don't you think?

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:36.950
I don't think I quite get it.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:40.290
And needless to say, 
there's also the cup ramen.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.800
Aside from the known 
manufacturers and store brands,

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:45.530
there are many brands made in
collaboration with famous restaurants.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:48.670
In my opinion, their soup's 
flavor fidelity is quite decent.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.960
Now that you mention it, I think 
I've heard of some of these places.

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:57.430
Incidentally, my current favorite is this 
simple dried sardine soy sauce ramen.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:01.970
I always buy a hot spring boiled egg and 
a packet of tempura flakes for topping.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:05.990
Once you add the egg, it does dilute 
the taste of the soup a bit,

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:08.840
so the trick is to add a little 
bit less water than normal.

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:12.320
The fishy broth and the tempura 
flakes go perfectly together.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.760
While it may seem like junk food,

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.930
it's quite close to the
 tsukimi tanuki udon experience.

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:24.520
The real pleasure of convenience store
ramen is the customization

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.710
you can do with the limited range
of items available here.

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:30.330
Thank you!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.670
<i>This is weird.</i>

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.580
<i>What's this cup ramen doing in front of me?</i>

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.760
Time to eat.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.880
<i>I had absolutely no appetite a minute ago.</i>

00:18:46.300 --> 00:18:49.770
Koizumi-san, do you ever worry about 
what you'll do after graduation?

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.110
<b>Tempura Flakes</b>

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:00.380
Thanks.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.260
Right, then. Let's eat.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.360
Time to eat.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.170
That'll be 165 yen.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:14.760
I'll pay with my phone.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:18.220
<i>Weird... Ramen is selling really well today.</i>

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:25.240
I figured she was going to eat more.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.780
<b>I knew it...</b>

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.720
She really is unwavering.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Tomato Ramen</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Euglena</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Huge Line</b>

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:16.640
Ah, I wonder where Koizumi-san is today.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:18.790
And now, a poem.

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:20.220
"Koizumi-san.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:22.160
Ah, Koizumi-san.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:23.320
Koizumi-san."

00:22:23.770 --> 00:22:25.850
Crap! The "n" of "san" is an extra syllable!

00:22:25.850 --> 00:22:27.870
Who cares about that?

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:29.990
I don't even have the energy to comment.

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:36.000
<b>Thank you for the meal!</b>
